.TH FASTCC 1.SH NAMEfastcc \- a faster front end for Microware's C compiler.SH SYNOPSIS\fBfastcc\fR[options] file ... [options].SH DESCRIPTION\fBfastcc\fRdrives Microware's C compiler passes -- the preprocessor, the compiler,the optimiser and the assembler and linker -- as\fBcc\fRdoes, with some options of its own and a choice of keeping theintermediate files in a directory you name.  It needs your own OS-9 Ccompiler installed..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-a\fRcompile to assembler files only..TP 12\fB\-r=\fIdir\fRcompile or assemble to relocatable files, in\fIdir\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-bp\fRshow each command before running it..TP 12\fB\-bg\fRmake the output a ghost module..TP 12\fB\-c\fRkeep comments in the assembler files..TP 12\fB\-d\fIname\fR, \-u\fIname\fRdefine or undefine a name for the preprocessor..TP 12\fB\-v=\fIdir\fRanother directory for the preprocessor to search..TP 12\fB\-e=\fIn\fRedition number of the output..TP 12\fB\-f=\fIpath\fR, \-fd=\fIpath\fRthe output path, in the execution or the data directory..TP 12\fB\-n=\fIname\fRthe output module's name..TP 12\fB\-g\fRdebugging information..TP 12\fB\-i\fRlink the clib trap library..TP 12\fB\-x\fRlink the math trap library..TP 12\fB\-l=\fIname\fRanother library to search..TP 12\fB\-j\fRno jump table..TP 12\fB\-s\fRno stack checking..TP 12\fB\-m=\fIn\fRextra stack memory in the output module..TP 12\fB\-o\fRdo not run the optimiser..TP 12\fB\-p\fRpipe the preprocessor's output straight into the compiler..TP 12\fB\-t=\fIdir\fRdirectory for temporary files..TP 12\fB\-q\fRquiet..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR